WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:08.074
Treating time as a resource starts with a simple fact: every hour is finite, nonrenewable, and already being spent somewhere.

2
00:00:08.074 --> 00:00:11.730
Time does not wait in storage until we feel ready to use it.

3
00:00:11.730 --> 00:00:19.728
It moves through work, learning, family life, operations, maintenance, recovery, and the small transitions between them.

4
00:00:19.728 --> 00:00:25.973
Resource thinking asks where that time is going, what it is supporting, and what else it prevents.

5
00:00:25.973 --> 00:00:30.772
Time is not the same thing as attention, energy, or calendar availability.

6
00:00:30.772 --> 00:00:37.475
A free hour after a difficult meeting may not have the same value as a protected hour at the start of the day.

7
00:00:37.475 --> 00:00:44.330
A person can technically have time and still lack the focus, context, or capacity to do demanding work well.

8
00:00:44.330 --> 00:00:51.490
That distinction matters because many planning failures begin by treating every open block as equally useful.

9
00:00:51.490 --> 00:00:55.146
This is not a guilt-based way to talk about productivity.

10
00:00:55.146 --> 00:01:01.696
The goal is not to shame people for rest, family commitments, interruptions, or imperfect execution.

11
00:01:01.696 --> 00:01:06.647
The goal is to make time allocation visible enough to manage it deliberately.

12
00:01:06.647 --> 00:01:09.541
When time use is invisible, defaults decide.

13
00:01:09.541 --> 00:01:18.834
Calendars fill, messages expand, urgent work crowds out important work, and people blame themselves for a system they never actually designed.

14
00:01:18.834 --> 00:01:22.033
A better frame is strategic resource management.

15
00:01:22.033 --> 00:01:29.726
Leaders, teams, students, parents, and individual contributors all make time tradeoffs whether they name them or not.

16
00:01:29.726 --> 00:01:34.525
The question is whether those tradeoffs support the outcomes that matter.

17
00:01:34.525 --> 00:01:38.409
Time can be planned, protected, reviewed, and reallocated.

18
00:01:38.409 --> 00:01:45.950
It cannot be recovered after it has been spent, which is why treating it as a resource changes the quality of decisions.
